~ father
if WorldState.has_flag("fl_met_father")
	Father: Back again. Good. The tide's kind this afternoon.
else
	do WorldState.set_flag("fl_met_father", true)
	Father: Well, hello there. We don't get many visitors out past the mangroves.
	Father: I'm a fisherman, mostly. Or something close to it. The boat does the real work.
Father: You can try the stones if you like. Flat ones skip best.
- Show me how.
	Father: Low and sideways, from the wrist. Don't throw it, let it go.
	Father: There. Three skips. Don't tell anyone I counted.
	do WorldState.set_flag("fl_skipped_stones", true)
- Who taught you?
	Father: Her mother, actually. She could get seven out of a flat stone, and she never once let me forget it.
	Father: It's all right. It's a good thing to remember.
	Father: My daughter has her wrist.
- I'd rather just sit for a while.
	Father: That's allowed. The beach isn't going anywhere.
	Father: There's lemonade up at the house when you want it. Key lime, from our own tree.
=> END

~ daughter
if WorldState.has_flag("fl_invited_to_horses")
	Daughter: Come on! They haven't had their brushing yet.
	=> END
Daughter: Hi! I've got two hundred stones in this bucket and I'm only allowed to keep fifty.
Daughter: Dad says I'm a collector, not a hoarder. I think that's just a nicer word.
- Which ones are your favorites?
	Daughter: The grey ones with a white stripe all the way around. Those are lucky.
	Daughter: You can have one. I've got four more.
- What else is out here?
	Daughter: Dolphins, if you wait. Crabs, always. A pelican who thinks he owns the dock.
	Daughter: And the horses, out back of the house. Do you like horses?
- I love horses.
	Daughter: Then you have to come see them! Wait. Hat.
	Daughter: Okay, got my hat. And my brush. Let's go!
	do WorldState.set_flag("fl_invited_to_horses", true)
- I've never really met one.
	Daughter: Oh, that's the best! They'll just stand there and let you be new.
	Daughter: Wait, hat. Okay. This way!
	do WorldState.set_flag("fl_invited_to_horses", true)
- Maybe later.
	Daughter: Okay! I'll be here. They'll be there. Nobody's in a hurry.
=> END
